Where they sit (drafter, `grep -n` at the sha): 174, 177 and 181 are inside `validateConditionWithAI` (`:5982`, begins `await aiGate.assertEnabled();` at `:5987`), the model-answered branch; the `getRuleBasedSuggestion(condition)` calls are at `:6224` and `:6285` (inside the same function) and the function itself is `:6414` (`const lowerCondition = condition.toLowerCase().trim();` at `:6415`), so 182 and 183 run only after a model answer has failed to produce a suggestion. The route is `app.post('/api/validate-condition'` at `:6836`; it calls `validateConditionWithAI` at `:6919` only after `aiGate.requireAiEnabled` (`:6915`). **The route's control-character check at `:6856` is `/[\u0000-\u0008\u000b\u000c\u000e-\u001f\u007f]/`: it refuses every C0 control EXCEPT TAB (0x09), LF (0x0A) and CR (0x0D), so a CR/LF condition reaches these sinks over HTTP** (the same fact the existing cell at `__tests__/rd774-risk-sql-templates.test.js:509` states). `generateKQLQueryForCondition` (`:5105`) strips characters outside `[a-zA-Z0-9\s%$.,()-]` at `:5109`: `\s` keeps CR and LF, so a CR/LF in the suggestion survives into the query text.
**What `logSafe` does to CR and LF (the drafter read `backend/logSafe.js` at the sha; you re-read it whole at Step 2):** `logSafe.js:34` `function logSafe(value, max = DEFAULT_MAX)`, `DEFAULT_MAX = 500` at `:29`; `:41` `s = s.replace(/\n|\r/g, '');` **REMOVES every CR and LF (an empty replacement, so the value is joined, not escaped)**; `:42` rewrites U+2028/U+2029 as visible `\uXXXX`; `:43` rewrites the other C0, DEL and C1 controls as `\xNN` (TAB kept); `:44` truncates past `max` with `…[+N chars]`. The header says the empty replacement is deliberate: it is the form CodeQL's barrier recognises. So the red cell is real because a raw `${value}` containing CR/LF followed by a forged text puts that text at the START of a log line, and `logSafe(value)` leaves it inside the one line.
**Two consequences you MEASURE and print, not assume (D2):** (1) a KQL query is multi-line by design (the base text `const baseKQL` at `:5117` onward has one clause per line), so `logSafe(kqlQuery)` logs it with its newlines removed (clauses joined, e.g. `...ago(30d)| extend...`), which changes the LOG TEXT of an ordinary query: that is inside "log output only" but the cell must say so and pin it; (2) the base query alone is longer than 500 characters, so the default `max` would CUT the logged query with `…[+N chars]`. The drafter's default for (2) is Q-1 of the report: pass an explicit `max` (a named constant above the longest query the function builds, measured by you over the route's returned `kqlQuery` for your cell inputs) so the log keeps the whole query; if you find a reason the default is better, STOP naming it. Lines 6184, 6242 and 6301 (`${aiSqlQuery}`, `${sqlQuery}`) are NOT in the five alerts at main and are NOT yours: record them under D8 only.

